unawaited(
  _persist().catchError((Object _) {
    // Best effort: the transcript stays in memory; the next trigger
    // retries the missed appends (see _persistedCount).
  }),
);
```

The same applies to three spots in the new test code (`_DeferredAppendEnv.appendFile`/`writeBinaryFile`/`createDir` signatures and the over-long `reason:` string at the "coalesced persist passes" test). Note `agent_service_persistence.dart` was formatter-clean on `main`, so this drift is introduced by this PR; `agent_service.dart` and the test file already carried drift on `main`, which is why this doesn't block.

Fix: `cd flutter_app && dart format lib/services/agent_service_persistence.dart test/agent_service_test.dart` and commit the result.

