♻️ **SUGGESTION: duplicated `ExecutionEnv` delegation boilerplate**

`_DeferredAppendEnv` re-implements the same ~75 lines of pass-through delegation that `_FailingSessionAppendEnv` (later in this very file) already provides: inner env, `cwd`, `absolutePath`, `joinPath`, `readTextFile`, `readBinaryFile`, `readTextLines`, `writeBinaryFile`, `writeFile`, `listDir`, `exists`, `createDir`, `remove`, `exec`. Similar wrappers also exist in `persistent_web_env_test.dart`, `ui/code_viewer_test.dart`, and `apps/apps_store_catalog_test.dart`.

Delegation itself is forced — `MemoryExecutionEnv` is a `final class`, so it can't be extended — but the mapping can be centralized in one place, e.g. a test-only base class with an overridable hook:

```dart
class _DelegatingEnv implements ExecutionEnv {
  _DelegatingEnv(this._inner);
  final ExecutionEnv _inner;
  // ...all pass-through members...

  // Override point: default = pass-through.
  Future<Result<void, FileError>> appendFile(String path, String content) =>
      _inner.appendFile(path, content);
}

class _DeferredAppendEnv extends _DelegatingEnv {
  _DeferredAppendEnv(super.inner);
  @override
  Future<Result<void, FileError>> appendFile(String path, String content) async {
    await Future<void>.delayed(Duration.zero);
    return super.appendFile(path, content);
  }
}
```

That removes ~70 lines here and lets `_FailingSessionAppendEnv` collapse to an override as well. Non-blocking: the PR follows the existing per-file-wrapper convention, so a follow-up refactor touching the other three files is also fine.

